// fixture-247: MAN-KDL-SYNTAX — 33 nested block comments exceed max nesting depth
//
// KDL 2.0 allows nested block comments (`/* /* */ */`).  The milpa depth guard
// tracks block-comment depth independently of brace depth, both capped at
// KDL_MAX_NESTING_DEPTH=32.  Input with 33 nested block comments (and ≤32 braces)
// MUST raise MAN-KDL-SYNTAX in BOTH implementations.
//
// Before fix (Rust-only): Rust's `kdl_brace_depth` guard only counted `{` / `}`;
// 33 block comments with no deep braces slipped past the guard → Rust parsed OK.
// Python's `_check_nesting_depth` already tracked both vectors → Python raised
// MAN-KDL-SYNTAX.  This was a cross-impl divergence.
//
// After fix: Rust's `kdl_block_comment_depth` guard is added alongside the brace
// guard; 33 nested block comments raise MAN-KDL-SYNTAX in both implementations.
name "x"
/* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* /* 33 nested block comments */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */ */
kind "library"
